<title>USA: Clinton to give &quot;encouraging news&quot; on budget.</title>
<headline>Clinton to give &quot;encouraging news&quot; on budget.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Clinton intends to use a formal news conference on Wednesday to disclose some &quot;encouraging news&quot; on efforts to balance the budget, Press Secretary Mike McCurry said.</p>
<p>Clinton plans to meet with reporters at 1400 EDT (1800 GMT) for an outdoor news conference at the White House.</p>
<p>He will announce &quot;some encouraging news on balancing the budget,&quot; McCurry said.</p>
<p>Fiscal forecasters have been revising downward their predictions on the size of the federal budget deficit for this year.</p>
</text>
